paras.en:
Enough, O despair; do not extinguish the heart so;
flash, O hope, at last show your gleam;
give a little comfort to the despairing;
come and increase the hearts of the depressed hearts.
By your breath life has come into the dead;
you have made the burnt crops green.

You were the ship for Noah in the flood;
you were the giver of peace to Jacob in Canaan;
you were the comforter of Zulaikha in separation;
you were the heart’s ease of Joseph in prison.
When calamities came and surrounded them,
the support there for all was you alone.

You have made many drowning ones float;
you have often set right the spoiled;
you have settled the uprooted hearts;
you have resettled the ruined homes.
